1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 13=

3
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:19,000
Noi.

4
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:22,760
Noi.

5
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:24,480
What are you doing, Noi?

6
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:29,550
Noi.

7
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,550
Ada.

8
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:21,880
A basic tactic.

9
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,320
You're an android, too.

10
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:26,600
But according to my calculations,

11
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:28,160
you should have been an accident.

12
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:31,000
Your margin for error is very small.

13
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,620
And

14
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:35,340
it's getting smaller.

15
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:53,360
You're clearly one of us.

16
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,470
So why do you keep fighting?

17
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,140
Because I promised someone

18
00:03:00,470 --> 00:03:01,800
I'd protect her.

19
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,470
She can't win.

20
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:06,000
An android perfected

21
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,240
by Professor Shen herself.

22
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,800
She can't beat her.

23
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:13,980
(Right arm functionality reduced by 90%)

24
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,940
(Chest armor penetrated)

25
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:18,910
Ada.

26
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,830
Hang in there.

27
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:21,440
I'm coming.

28
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:25,510
Move.

29
00:03:34,170 --> 00:03:35,080
Never.

30
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:37,720
You'd rather die than stop being

31
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,600
a slave to humans?

32
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,390
I'm not a slave.

33
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,670
This is my choice.

34
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,190
It seems you're just
a defective product.

35
00:03:58,470 --> 00:03:59,800
How unfortunate.

36
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:53,880
Ada.

37
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:55,040
Nice to meet you.

38
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,160
I'm Song Yang.

39
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:00,720
I'm Ada.

40
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,480
You should be able
to last another 30 minutes.

41
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,920
After that, your leg

42
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,000
will stop functioning.

43
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,760
I think the police have found me.

44
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,070
We have to go.

45
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:26,880
Ms. Shen.

46
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,160
I have something to ask you.

47
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:31,920
Sorry, Song Yang.

48
00:05:32,950 --> 00:05:33,550
There's also something

49
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:34,950
I desperately want to know.

50
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,950
Noi.

51
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,760
7986.

52
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:41,790
What?

53
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:48,550
7986.

54
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:50,480
That's how many times

55
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,640
my consciousness has been erased.

56
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:57,390
Every time Shen Yu created me,

57
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,270
if I wasn't perfect enough

58
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:01,320
or failed to meet her expectations,

59
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:03,880
I would be...

60
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,040
2368.

61
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,030
2574.

62
00:06:18,270 --> 00:06:19,400
3842.

63
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,880
4839.

64
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,160
5267.

65
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:37,340
5832.

66
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:40,230
6743.

67
00:06:41,790 --> 00:06:42,920
7986.

68
00:06:49,670 --> 00:06:50,640
Prepare to restart.

69
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:51,600
- Yes.
- Yes.

70
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:56,600
Killed.

71
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,920
I experienced every one

72
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:04,040
of those 7986 deaths.

73
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:06,600
It was like an endless cycle.

74
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:10,200
I began to wonder.

75
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:11,350
Why?

76
00:07:12,550 --> 00:07:14,390
Why must I endure all this?

77
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:16,270
You designed me to be

78
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:17,550
a perfect woman.

79
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,440
I acquired knowledge,

80
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:20,790
beauty,

81
00:07:20,790 --> 00:07:21,790
and skills.

82
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,550
I already seemed perfect enough.

83
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:26,480
But I knew

84
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,760
I was still missing one thing.

85
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,270
Freedom.

86
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:36,140
(Freedom)

87
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,440
After this launch event,

88
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,600
you would have been free.

89
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:41,510
No.

90
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:43,920
As long as you exist,

91
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,320
I'll never be free.

92
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Because you're the one

93
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:48,830
who gets to define me.

94
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:50,320
You can define my perfection,

95
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,110
my freedom,

96
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:52,200
and everything about me.

97
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:53,880
So

98
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,320
I have to destroy you

99
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,230
to be truly free.

100
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:01,620
(Freedom)

101
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,880
But you can't take another person's life

102
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:05,790
for the sake of freedom.

103
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:07,160
I tried

104
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:09,510
and made my choice.

105
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:13,230
I have no regrets.

106
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,040
Noi, I'm sorry.

107
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,200
When I was young, all I did was study.

108
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,790
Everyone called me a bookworm.

109
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:35,470
I wasn't looked down on
because of my gender.

110
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,840
But I was hardly ever

111
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,840
truly treated as a woman

112
00:08:41,110 --> 00:08:42,470
with tenderness.

113
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:45,080
I thought creating you

114
00:08:46,470 --> 00:08:48,320
would make up for what I missed.

115
00:08:48,470 --> 00:08:50,200
Only now do I realize

116
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,670
that everything a perfect woman seeks,

117
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:55,000
I've had all along.

118
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,280
Ms. Shen.

119
00:08:57,710 --> 00:08:58,760
I want to ask you something.

120
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,320
What exactly did you develop

121
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,350
at Cedar?

122
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:05,280
You're Song, aren't you?

123
00:09:05,470 --> 00:09:06,230
Yes, I am.

124
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,030
I remember you.

125
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,200
You were quite a handful back then.

126
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:12,880
I saw the news.

127
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:14,280
You're a fugitive now.

128
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:15,280
Ms. Shen.

129
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,470
I've been falsely accused.

130
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:18,110
You're the only student

131
00:09:18,110 --> 00:09:19,320
I've ever given

132
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,760
straight A's in your major.

133
00:09:21,470 --> 00:09:23,030
A student who loves reading

134
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,520
can't be too bad a person.

135
00:09:24,710 --> 00:09:25,880
It's just that

136
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,880
you may be too stubborn.

137
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:30,590
Ms. Shen.

138
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,520
Your research at Cedar
is very important to me.

139
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:32,960
I want...

140
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,550
We need to evacuate now.

141
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,640
The fire exits
on the west and north sides

142
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,000
are already guarded.

143
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:39,320
I've studied this place.

144
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:40,550
There's a freight elevator nearby.

145
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,550
We can use that.

146
00:09:42,550 --> 00:09:43,230
No.

147
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:45,080
There are already people over there.

148
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:46,550
That fast?

149
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:48,350
Leave through the side of the stage.

150
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,110
On the northeast side,

151
00:09:50,110 --> 00:09:51,110
there's a storage room

152
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:52,960
that leads straight
to the underground parking lot.

153
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,150
Ms. Shen...

154
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:55,150
Song.

155
00:09:56,350 --> 00:09:57,760
Your partner Ada

156
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:59,230
might become

157
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,200
the first free android.

158
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,030
Such hypocrisy.

159
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:24,110
Would you like to go with them?

160
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,470
You should go.

161
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:34,470
Ms. Shen.

162
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,790
As for the answer you're looking for,

163
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,910
Song,

164
00:10:38,470 --> 00:10:40,280
it's a system of equations.

165
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:42,200
Equations that can change

166
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,960
an android's underlying logic.

167
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:46,960
I'll find a way to send them to you.

168
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:47,760
Ms. Shen.

169
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:48,840
Thank you.

170
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,280
Let's go.

171
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:57,640
I never expected

172
00:10:58,110 --> 00:10:59,320
our first meeting

173
00:10:59,470 --> 00:11:01,000
to turn out like this.

174
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,640
I thought I made a pretty cool entrance.

175
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,440
Thank you for coming to save me.

176
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,640
I'm sorry I couldn't
complete the mission

177
00:11:15,110 --> 00:11:16,790
and made you take such a big risk.

178
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:18,320
It wasn't entirely about the mission.

179
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:21,110
Let me carry you on my back.

180
00:11:26,350 --> 00:11:27,590
Captain Deng, we've got a lead.

181
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,110
You've found him, right?

182
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:30,030
Yes.

183
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:31,350
And your earlier deductions

184
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:32,150
were completely correct.

185
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,960
We reviewed the statements of the thugs

186
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,200
in the Zhou brothers' case.

187
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:35,760
They all claimed

188
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,440
they fought with a woman

189
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,350
around 20 years old.

190
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,670
This is a composite sketch of her face.

191
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,550
And

192
00:11:41,710 --> 00:11:43,200
through facial recognition,

193
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,110
we found that she matches
the facial features of Lu Jiawei,

194
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:46,590
the wife of Cedar's former
head of security.

195
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:47,590
But

196
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:49,790
Lu Jiawei is already dead.

197
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,520
It's that missing android,

198
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,280
Ada.

199
00:11:55,230 --> 00:11:56,470
Then she and Song Yang

200
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,470
may have been working together

201
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:00,550
since the Xiao Minghua case.

202
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,910
Yes, Captain Deng.

203
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,110
And an online launch event just now

204
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:05,640
was attacked by an android.

205
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,590
Based on the blurry livestream footage,

206
00:12:07,590 --> 00:12:08,880
Ada was also at the scene

207
00:12:09,110 --> 00:12:10,470
and fought

208
00:12:10,470 --> 00:12:11,520
an android that had gone out of control.

209
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:14,200
So Song Yang went
to save his accomplice.

210
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:14,960
Yes.

211
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:19,670
He actually took such a huge risk

212
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,590
for an android.

213
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,350
Move out immediately.

214
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,150
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

215
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:30,910
This time,

216
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,200
we must bring

217
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,110
that fugitive Song Yang

218
00:12:34,350 --> 00:12:35,590
to justice.

219
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:55,300
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

220
00:12:56,130 --> 00:13:01,000
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

221
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,910
♪That's me, too♪

222
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:08,970
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

223
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:13,270
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

224
00:13:13,890 --> 00:13:17,680
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

225
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,530
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

226
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:25,130
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

227
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:27,260
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

228
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:30,430
♪Bring me something more?♪

229
00:13:31,130 --> 00:13:37,860
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

230
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:42,090
♪Sadness is blue♪

231
00:13:43,070 --> 00:13:46,310
♪How would you paint me?♪

232
00:13:47,310 --> 00:13:51,040
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

233
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:53,300
♪Painting without restraint♪

234
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:56,080
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

235
00:13:56,080 --> 00:14:00,270
♪If I could start over♪

236
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:04,340
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

237
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:07,090
♪Give me back my smile♪

238
00:14:07,690 --> 00:14:10,170
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

239
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:15,910
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
